  "body": [
    {
      "_key": "en",
      "_type": "object",
      "value": [
        {
          "_key": "000000000001",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "ohnl0i9ib6pr",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Getting Around "
            },
            {
              "_key": "nqpvbh3sexpw",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong",
                "5qa773ttama9"
              ],
              "text": "Suez"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "5qa773ttama9",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58938",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000003",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Understanding the Accommodation Landscape"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000005",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "8t29u7m8jddr",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Suez is an industrial port city and the southern gateway to the Suez Canal. It is not a tourist destination in the conventional sense, and the city itself has very limited visitor accommodation — mainstream booking platforms list essentially no hotels within Suez city centre. Visitors who need to stay in the city for canal-related business, transit purposes, or independent travel typically rely on budget guesthouses and smaller local properties that do not appear in international booking systems. Your best approach is to ask locally or through your travel contacts on arrival, or to base yourself in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "m77k8dscyswx",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "ty7no4uzb7c5"
              ],
              "text": "Ismailia"
            },
            {
              "_key": "dro0fmo8mgrt",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " (the most visitor-friendly of the three Canal Zone cities, roughly 80km north) and make Suez a day trip."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "ty7no4uzb7c5",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58868",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "The hotels that do appear under “Suez” searches are almost entirely located in "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ain Sokhna"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", a Red Sea resort corridor stretching from roughly 40km to 100km south of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000009"
              ],
              "text": "Suez city"
            },
            {
              "_key": "xoyptf05ueph",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " along the Suez–"
            },
            {
              "_key": "sefob245yceh",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "rxfhkspg9w76"
              ],
              "text": "Hurghada"
            },
            {
              "_key": "7wyjgm8t0k7a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " road. Ain Sokhna is a popular weekend and holiday destination for Cairenes — it sits about 120km from "
            },
            {
              "_key": "geo5luzu3f72",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "ldi7wjfj9nk8"
              ],
              "text": "Cairo"
            },
            {
              "_key": "z8fsyx1xk14l",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " — and its resorts are genuine Red Sea properties with beaches, pools, and full amenities. They are well-suited to a beach holiday or a weekend break from Cairo. They are not well-suited to visitors who need early-morning bus connections from Suez, want to watch shipping traffic in the canal, or are passing through on a longer itinerary."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_pendingInternalRef": {
                "sourceLocale": "en",
                "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/suez-travel-guide/"
              },
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "/guide/suez",
              "newTab": false
            },
            {
              "_key": "rxfhkspg9w76",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58859",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            },
            {
              "_key": "ldi7wjfj9nk8",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-83284",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ain Sokhna: Red Sea Resorts"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "If a Red Sea beach stay near the northern Gulf of Suez is what you are looking for, Ain Sokhna has a well-developed resort offering. The following properties have consistent reputations:"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000013",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Stella Di Mare Sea Club Hotel"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " (Km 46, Suez–Hurghada Road) is a mid-range beach resort with an outdoor pool, spa, diving and watersports, and Mediterranean and Far Eastern cuisine restaurants. It sits at the northern end of the Ain Sokhna stretch and is the closest of the major resorts to Suez city."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Mövenpick Resort El Sokhna"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " (Km 64, Suez–Hurghada Road) is a five-star property with a private beach, three restaurants, and extensive gardens set against the Attaka mountains. It is approximately 1.5 hours from Cairo International Airport and is the most internationally recognised resort in the area."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000019",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Teda Swiss Inn Plaza Hotel & Aqua Park"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " is located at the entrance to the Chinese-Egyptian Economic Zone (TEDA), between Ain Sokhna and Suez city, and markets itself to both leisure and business visitors given its access to the industrial zone. It includes a water park, spa, and fitness centre."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Cancun Sokhna Resort"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " (Km 102, Zafarana Road) is at the southern end of the Ain Sokhna stretch, significantly further from Suez city and closer to the midpoint between Suez and Hurghada. It offers five restaurants, a kids’ club, and direct beach access."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Practical Notes for Canal Zone Visitors"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000022",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000001f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Visitors primarily interested in the Suez Canal itself — the canal monument, the viewing areas, the atmosphere of a major working port — may find "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000020",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ismailia"
            },
            {
              "_key": "gfz44nf43znz",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " a more rewarding base. Ismailia sits on the western bank of the canal midway along its length, has a more pleasant urban character than Suez city, and has the Mercure Forsan Island Hotel and a handful of other properties on or near Lake Timsah. From Ismailia you can reach both Suez and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "pafjbz2owajh",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "sg76dz9363cg"
              ],
              "text": "Port Said"
            },
            {
              "_key": "v12x0z0wdgli",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " by bus in approximately one hour."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "sg76dz9363cg",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58900",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000024",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000023",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "For anyone transiting through Suez on a longer Egypt itinerary — arriving by bus and departing early the next morning — the practical reality is that budget accommodation options exist in the city but are not well-documented online. The bus station area and the city centre have local guesthouses; ask at the bus station or at a local café for current recommendations."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000026",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000025",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "em"
              ],
              "text": "Updated: March 2026"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
